{
  "description": "Destinations a gateway may connect to, RELAY-v0.md section 3 (the rule on addresses of the gateway). Each case: the address of the connection a gateway is about to open (to fetch metadata, for enrollment or for the tunnel), after the name was resolved, as text; and whether the gateway connects (allow) or refuses (refuse). A gateway connects only to globally reachable unicast addresses, as the IANA special-purpose address registries define them, with these additions: an IPv4-mapped address and an IPv4-compatible address and an address of 2002::/16 are never allowed; of IPv6 only 2000::/3 is allowed, and as the one exception 64:ff9b::/96, which is allowed only if the IPv4 address in its last 32 bits is allowed (64:ff9b:1::/48 is not). A text that is not an IPv4 address in dotted decimal or an IPv6 address is refused (d84 to d95 include spellings of other tools: numbers, octal and hexadecimal parts, brackets, white space and a trailing dot). The cases show decisions, not that an implementation is general.",
